From: kudanilmakantahwu <kudanilmakantahwu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:20:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] gallium/dri: advertise EGL_OPENGL_ES_BIT when ES2 is present

Mesa 26.3 gates GLES1 behind HAVE_OPENGL_ES_1, which the Arch build
disables.  driCreateNewScreen2() therefore leaves max_gl_es1_version at 0
and clears the __DRI_API_GLES bit from screen->api_mask, so
dri2_setup_screen() no longer reports EGL_OPENGL_ES_BIT in the display's
ClientAPIs.

eglChooseConfig() treats an omitted EGL_RENDERABLE_TYPE as
EGL_OPENGL_ES_BIT (EGL 1.5, table 3.4).  GTK 4 builds its config
attribute list without that attribute, so with no ES_BIT config
advertised eglChooseConfig() returns zero configs and GTK falls back to
the cairo software renderer ("No EGL configuration available").

Advertise the legacy GLES1 API bit whenever ES2 or newer is available so
ES_BIT configs exist again.  A freedreno GLES1 context is still not
reachable (max_gl_es1_version stays 0); the ES_BIT config is only what
GTK needs in order to pick a real ES2/GL context.

--- a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_util.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_util.c
@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@
        screen->api_mask |= (1 << __DRI_API_OPENGL);
     if (screen->max_gl_core_version > 0)
        screen->api_mask |= (1 << __DRI_API_OPENGL_CORE);
-    if (screen->max_gl_es1_version > 0)
+    if (screen->max_gl_es1_version > 0 || screen->max_gl_es2_version > 0)
        screen->api_mask |= (1 << __DRI_API_GLES);
     if (screen->max_gl_es2_version > 0)
        screen->api_mask |= (1 << __DRI_API_GLES2);
